 "result_text": "`HttpTransport` no longer uses `Hub`. I removed the `Hub` import and the `hub_cls` attribute from `__init__` in `sentry_sdk/transport.py`. I also removed the `with hub:` wrapper in `capture_envelope`. The send function now just runs `_send_envelope` and `_flush_client_reports` inside `capture_internal_exceptions()`.\n\n`tests/test_transport.py` gives 45 passed and 32 skipped, because eventlet and gevent aren't installed. I didn't run the rest of the test suite.\n\nNothing else in the SDK referenced `hub_cls`. The wrapper used to activate the captured hub in the worker thread, so there's no longer any hub or scope context in that thread. I didn't add scope handling to replace it.",
